WEBVTT

00:04.820 --> 00:07.070
Tell me something, Nanase.

00:08.530 --> 00:13.730
Tsukishiro said he'd sent a student 
from the White Room as an assassin.

00:14.040 --> 00:15.790
Was that all a bluff?

00:16.460 --> 00:19.120
I don't know what that means.

00:19.360 --> 00:25.000
I don't know much about 
the White Room myself.

00:25.520 --> 00:28.290
<i>She doesn't appear to be lying.</i>

00:28.290 --> 00:32.720
<i>And she's not competent enough 
to be the assassin herself.</i>

00:33.560 --> 00:35.080
<i>Which means...</i>

00:37.000 --> 00:40.160
Looks like we're in for 
a real downpour, huh,

00:40.720 --> 00:43.020
Senpai?

00:52.570 --> 00:58.370
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:02.450 --> 02:09.000
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:15.700 --> 02:18.110
<b>#13 Obscured By the Rain</b>

02:15.990 --> 02:18.490
Get behind me.

02:18.490 --> 02:19.680
Oh?

02:19.680 --> 02:23.000
Nanase-chan, you're not happy to see me?

02:23.000 --> 02:26.740
What an awful way to treat 
your own groupmate...

02:26.740 --> 02:31.760
Or did this little guy here 
make me look threatening?

02:31.760 --> 02:33.760
I can't trust you.

02:33.760 --> 02:35.760
Not nice!

02:36.360 --> 02:38.560
Why would you even say that?

02:38.560 --> 02:40.640
I'm such a li'l cutie pie!

02:41.640 --> 02:44.480
Seriously, I'm not a bad girl.

02:44.480 --> 02:46.640
Right, Ayanokoji-senpai?

02:47.020 --> 02:49.400
Let's talk a while.

02:49.620 --> 02:53.260
Senpai, there's something 
I haven't told you about.

02:54.400 --> 02:57.850
After the rest of you went 
looking for Shinohara-senpai,

02:57.850 --> 03:02.790
I sensed someone watching us 
and chased after them.

03:03.080 --> 03:06.080
They ran, so I was unable 
to catch up with them,

03:06.400 --> 03:08.790
but they had a distinct hairstyle.

03:08.790 --> 03:10.290
Amasawa-san.

03:10.650 --> 03:13.550
You hurt Komiya-senpai and 
Kinoshita-senpai, didn't you?

03:16.050 --> 03:18.230
Let me turn that one around on you.

03:18.230 --> 03:21.870
If it turned out I <i>did</i> do it...

03:21.870 --> 03:23.560
What would you do?

03:23.850 --> 03:25.620
I'd want to know why you did it.

03:26.060 --> 03:32.070
More importantly... why didn't your 
name show up on the GPS tracker?

03:32.070 --> 03:35.550
Erasing your presence isn't 
difficult in and of itself.

03:35.900 --> 03:38.450
You just have to damage your watch.

03:38.450 --> 03:42.060
You heard him, Nanase-chan.

03:43.580 --> 03:45.650
Why have you come here?

03:45.650 --> 03:49.320
Or rather... how exactly did you find us?

03:49.320 --> 03:52.920
Slow down now, Ayanokoji-senpai.

03:52.920 --> 03:55.840
Let's savor the fact that 
we found each other at all.

03:56.150 --> 04:00.090
I'm sorry, but I'd like to keep 
this brief, given the rain and all.

04:00.310 --> 04:04.820
Then how about we have a 
sleepover chat in your tent?

04:05.850 --> 04:07.830
Hands-on contact, huh?

04:07.830 --> 04:11.980
I want to talk to Ayanokoji-senpai. 
Step aside, please.

04:11.980 --> 04:14.320
You can talk right here.

04:14.320 --> 04:16.610
No, I don't think we can.

04:16.610 --> 04:21.130
We'll be talking about 
the White Room, see?

04:21.680 --> 04:25.740
You get it now, little Miss Outsider?

04:29.670 --> 04:30.500
Sorry,

04:30.730 --> 04:34.900
but I won't believe you're from the 
White Room just because you know about it.

04:35.400 --> 04:38.350
What would you gain from 
revealing your identity?

04:38.350 --> 04:40.040
What do I gain?

04:40.040 --> 04:44.890
I wanted to let you know 
that I'm not your enemy.

04:45.130 --> 04:46.770
That doesn't add up.

04:47.130 --> 04:52.150
The White Room student is an assassin 
sent here to get me expelled.

04:52.420 --> 04:55.260
To say that you're not my enemy 
isn't logically consistent.

04:55.580 --> 04:57.850
I'm sure he thought a White Room student

04:57.850 --> 05:02.410
would happily expel you out of jealousy.

05:02.630 --> 05:06.320
But he didn't anticipate that I'd be a

05:06.320 --> 05:11.290
pure-hearted young maiden bursting 
with admiration for you!

05:11.530 --> 05:17.170
Then why didn't you reveal all this the 
moment you arrived at the school?

05:17.170 --> 05:24.540
Because, as much as I admired you, 
I'd never actually met you.

05:24.540 --> 05:29.680
I needed time to watch you and see if 
that "Oh, I'm so glad I admired him!"

05:30.030 --> 05:33.190
reaction was in the cards.

05:33.590 --> 05:36.410
If you had the same upbringing I did,

05:36.410 --> 05:39.940
I suppose you've realized how 
interesting this school is, too?

05:40.300 --> 05:45.790
Yeah, I've thought plenty about 
how much I'd love to stay here and

05:45.790 --> 05:47.920
enjoy myself until graduation.

05:48.380 --> 05:53.580
Though I'm awful at making friends, 
so I don't have many people to talk to.

05:53.800 --> 06:00.460
But I'm not totally lacking in 
communication skills like you are.

06:00.960 --> 06:05.010
There are things only the fifth class, 
one year below yours, is learning:

06:05.710 --> 06:10.670
the ability to hold a basic conversation.

06:10.670 --> 06:14.560
As a member of the fourth class, 
you're surely aware that its focus

06:14.560 --> 06:18.110
on pure individualism crushed 
nearly everyone in it.

06:18.110 --> 06:20.190
I believe your story now.

06:20.620 --> 06:25.240
But I don't feel you've adequately 
explained why you've revealed yourself.

06:25.480 --> 06:28.860
You seem pretty calm for 
someone who just accepted

06:28.860 --> 06:30.660
that I'm a White Room student.

06:30.990 --> 06:35.000
Maybe you think I can't 
be a threat to you?

06:36.630 --> 06:40.050
Oh, well... I've told 
you what I wanted to,

06:40.050 --> 06:42.130
so I think I'll be on my way.

06:44.940 --> 06:49.740
Don't go getting crushed without 
my permission, all right?

06:55.620 --> 06:57.040
Are you all right?

06:58.480 --> 06:59.730
Senpai?

07:02.230 --> 07:05.760
Are those Amasawa-san's tracks?

07:05.760 --> 07:10.740
Yes. There were tracks nearby when 
Komiya and Kinoshita were injured.

07:11.090 --> 07:14.620
The size is about the same as 
Amasawa's, so I can be certain.

07:15.940 --> 07:19.780
Amasawa seems to have 
approached me from behind...

07:22.630 --> 07:27.260
But when the tracks get closer 
to us, they become scrambled.

07:28.190 --> 07:33.100
And then the set of mystery tracks 
turns back for some reason.

07:33.340 --> 07:40.460
Someone else was here before 
Amasawa-san called out to us, you mean?

07:40.460 --> 07:47.860
Yes. And this stick has been 
trimmed for use as a weapon.

07:48.260 --> 07:53.320
If Amasawa had wanted to attack me, 
she should have ambushed me.

07:53.760 --> 07:57.500
However, she showed no sign of hostility.

07:57.800 --> 08:03.850
So it wasn't Amasawa-san who brought this 
stick, but whoever made these tracks?

08:04.470 --> 08:06.510
But why...

08:06.510 --> 08:10.890
Amasawa said she admired me.

08:11.210 --> 08:16.620
If she thought I was about to 
be attacked, it makes sense that

08:16.620 --> 08:18.160
she would protect me.

08:18.160 --> 08:23.820
Declaring her an ally based on 
only that feels dangerous to me.

08:24.090 --> 08:26.080
Either way, the situation is what it is.

08:26.560 --> 08:28.860
Let's set up the tents quickly.

08:33.690 --> 08:36.080
"To make up for the suspension of the test,

08:35.330 --> 08:42.960
Advanced Nurturing High School Management
Due to today's suspension of testing due to poor weather,
only 1/4 of movement and challenge tasks were able
to be completed. The final day's arrival bonuses,
arrival order rewards, and challenge rewards will all be
doubled to compensate for this loss in points.
The weather is expected to improve tomorrow morning.

08:36.080 --> 08:39.560
all rewards on the last 
day will be doubled."

08:39.920 --> 08:42.960
That could result in dramatic comebacks.

08:43.370 --> 08:48.290
They've also given us time to consider 
how to plan for the late game.

08:48.920 --> 08:50.010
Senpai.

08:52.160 --> 08:53.600
Nanase?

08:53.820 --> 08:57.380
I want to talk to you. May I come in?

08:58.540 --> 09:01.850
So? What did you want to 
talk about in the rain?

09:02.600 --> 09:07.530
I was certain that Amasawa-san 
had pushed those two students,

09:07.530 --> 09:10.990
but you don't seem to 
think that's a guarantee.

09:11.270 --> 09:16.180
There's no way to confirm if 
Amasawa did anything to them,

09:16.180 --> 09:19.630
but I've more or less figured 
out who's on what table.

09:21.100 --> 09:24.560
On the sixth day, when GPS search 
restrictions were lifted,

09:24.560 --> 09:26.750
I conducted ten such searches.

09:27.400 --> 09:32.020
It's an extremely useful tool to 
learn where other students are.

09:32.020 --> 09:34.230
I'm sorry if this is a rude question,

09:34.230 --> 09:37.510
but was that really worth 
spending ten game points on?

09:37.510 --> 09:41.830
Each GPS search does cost 
one game point, true,

09:41.830 --> 09:44.770
and a single usage is far from effective.

09:44.770 --> 09:50.050
However, repeated searches 
allowed me to connect the dots

09:50.050 --> 09:52.680
and see patterns I hadn't noticed before.

09:53.040 --> 09:56.340
For instance, there are a 
number of third-year groups

09:53.910 --> 09:55.240
Nagumo G

09:55.160 --> 09:56.870
Nagumo G

09:55.160 --> 09:56.870
Kiriyama G

09:56.340 --> 10:00.540
that are always sticking close to 
the Nagumo and Kiriyama groups.

09:56.780 --> 09:58.490
Nagumo G

09:56.780 --> 09:58.490
Kiriyama G

09:58.410 --> 10:00.000
Nagumo G

09:58.410 --> 10:00.000
Kiriyama G

09:59.910 --> 10:00.540
Nagumo G

09:59.910 --> 10:00.540
Kiriyama G

10:01.120 --> 10:04.960
They're likely arranging things 
in advance so that Nagumo

10:04.960 --> 10:08.300
effortlessly takes first place in 
any challenge he participates in.

10:08.920 --> 10:11.140
We can assume the groups 
cooperating with Nagumo

10:11.140 --> 10:14.110
are being made to compete 
among themselves.

10:14.560 --> 10:17.280
Nagumo has probably also 
prepared his own method

10:17.280 --> 10:19.820
to avoid expulsion in an emergency.

10:20.340 --> 10:23.690
It's like the student council president 
is holding a test of his own.

10:23.970 --> 10:27.790
Nagumo has his entire class year 
under his thumb, after all.

10:27.790 --> 10:31.070
As one of the people who makes the rules.

10:32.490 --> 10:34.920
<i>Of course, like Nagumo,</i>

10:34.920 --> 10:39.200
<i>a small group of second-years are taking 
a strategy of helping each other.</i>

10:39.500 --> 10:43.490
<i>But unlike Nagumo, 
we negotiated that as equals.</i>

10:44.010 --> 10:47.650
<i>One thing the second-year 
leaders have going for them</i>

10:47.650 --> 10:50.980
<i>is the ability to work together 
when their interests align.</i>

10:51.520 --> 10:55.720
I can see why that information was 
worth spending ten game points for.

10:56.110 --> 11:00.410
The minute the rain stops, 
I'm going to go after Amasawa-san.

11:00.410 --> 11:03.860
Now that she's made it clear 
she's a White Room student,

11:03.860 --> 11:06.050
I'm worried about what she'll do next.

11:06.390 --> 11:08.680
I wouldn't recommend that.

11:08.680 --> 11:11.860
Focus on protecting yourself, not me.

11:12.110 --> 11:14.410
I'm not afraid of being expelled.

11:14.410 --> 11:18.240
I intend to do whatever 
it takes to protect you.

11:18.710 --> 11:20.870
Allow me to rephrase.

11:20.870 --> 11:23.350
Having you out there 
acting as a wild card

11:23.350 --> 11:26.000
could hinder me in unexpected ways.

11:26.590 --> 11:29.930
I'd like you to avoid making risky moves.

11:31.380 --> 11:33.600
True... I wouldn't want to do that.

11:34.250 --> 11:37.260
I don't want to make any 
more trouble for you.

11:37.630 --> 11:40.850
Besides, Hosen's in your group, too.

11:40.850 --> 11:44.020
Be careful moving forward. All right?

11:44.270 --> 11:46.850
Very well. I promise I will.

11:50.230 --> 11:53.640
I suppose this is goodbye 
for a while, then?

12:05.300 --> 12:06.750
Ayanokoji-kun?

12:08.150 --> 12:09.660
I haven't seen you since the first day.

12:11.300 --> 12:13.500
You're in better shape than I expected.

12:13.870 --> 12:15.480
Are you still on your own?

12:15.480 --> 12:19.760
I've faced my share of adversity, 
but it also makes many things easier.

12:20.010 --> 12:22.630
Did you hear about Shinohara's group?

12:22.630 --> 12:23.640
Yes.

12:23.640 --> 12:26.890
Sakayanagi-san just 
told me about it today.

12:26.890 --> 12:30.230
So you didn't refuse her offer?

12:30.230 --> 12:32.150
I had no reason to do so.

12:32.570 --> 12:35.610
Shinohara-san's group is currently 
seventh from the bottom.

12:35.940 --> 12:40.290
If she can't find a group to 
join up with, I'll take action.

12:40.290 --> 12:44.410
Luckily, I've managed to open three 
group slots through challenge success.

12:44.410 --> 12:50.080
But then you and Shinohara-san will have 
to get game points all by yourselves.

12:50.080 --> 12:54.040
I'd prefer to have them absorbed by 
a group with lots of game points.

12:54.270 --> 12:55.260
Yes.

12:55.260 --> 13:00.680
Still, I've become keenly aware of the 
number of groups that have transceivers.

13:00.680 --> 13:04.150
That does seem common among 
the well-organized upper classes

13:04.150 --> 13:06.810
with lots of points to spend.

13:07.260 --> 13:13.060
Could we have done the same if 
we'd trusted each other a bit more?

13:13.060 --> 13:16.060
It could also prove a waste of resources.

13:16.060 --> 13:18.820
It won't necessarily help them.

13:19.120 --> 13:20.220
True.

13:25.300 --> 13:27.130
<i>My total game points 
are just a hair behind</i>

13:27.130 --> 13:29.100
<i>those of the tenth-place Kuronaga group.</i>

13:29.560 --> 13:33.930
<i>The important thing is to 
stay just below tenth place.</i>

13:34.580 --> 13:36.710
<i>If I enter the top ten and stand out,</i>

13:36.710 --> 13:39.940
<i>it raises the chances of rivals 
attempting to hinder me.</i>

13:40.340 --> 13:45.850
<i>I want to maintain my ideal placement 
and get in touch with Sakayanagi soon.</i>

13:51.100 --> 13:53.100
Is anyone in there?

13:55.860 --> 13:59.690
Sorry, but I'll be setting 
up my tent nearby.

13:59.690 --> 14:01.610
If you have a problem 
with that, let me know.

14:07.120 --> 14:10.460
I was wondering what kind of 
freak showed up. So it was you.

14:12.620 --> 14:14.430
Was I making too much noise?

14:14.430 --> 14:15.630
Nah.

14:25.580 --> 14:26.800
May I come in?

14:26.800 --> 14:28.850
I want to ask you something.

14:29.980 --> 14:32.020
I'm opening up. Is that okay?

14:34.820 --> 14:36.610
What's that you're eating?

14:37.660 --> 14:38.860
Jerky.

14:38.860 --> 14:43.240
Jerky? That wasn't in the 
manual we were given.

14:43.240 --> 14:44.990
So what?

14:44.990 --> 14:46.870
It's none of your business.

14:50.800 --> 14:52.000
What are you doing?!

14:52.000 --> 14:54.000
Your pulse is racing.

14:54.000 --> 14:56.090
Your lips are parched, as well.

14:56.090 --> 14:58.220
Clear signs of dehydration.

14:58.960 --> 15:02.510
I'm not thirsty... anymore.

15:02.510 --> 15:06.240
"Anymore" suggests you 
were thirsty before.

15:06.240 --> 15:07.840
It's none of your business!

15:08.240 --> 15:10.430
I'm doing just fine.

15:12.350 --> 15:14.540
Hey! Don't you touch—

15:14.940 --> 15:16.810
How long have you gone without water?

15:17.030 --> 15:18.810
I don't have to tell you anything.

15:18.810 --> 15:20.440
How long?

15:22.040 --> 15:24.950
A little over a day.

15:24.950 --> 15:27.760
And you've been walking around like that?

15:27.760 --> 15:30.340
I can always go back to the 
starting point if I have to.

15:30.340 --> 15:31.330
Leave me alone.

15:31.330 --> 15:33.360
That's quite far from here.

15:33.680 --> 15:35.960
If you collapse on the 
way, you're finished.

15:35.960 --> 15:38.830
Then I'll win a challenge or something!

15:38.830 --> 15:42.590
If it were that simple, 
you wouldn't be struggling now.

15:47.290 --> 15:48.440
Let's make a trade.

15:48.790 --> 15:49.840
What?

15:49.840 --> 15:52.690
I'm running low on food myself.

15:53.160 --> 15:55.980
And I have a bit more water than I need.

15:56.430 --> 16:01.950
I think we can make a trade on even 
terms, so I'd like to negotiate.

16:03.220 --> 16:07.420
Well? Once again, I'm offering 
a trade on even terms.

16:07.420 --> 16:09.830
In exchange for this, 
I'd like some of your food.

16:09.830 --> 16:11.870
Hell no.

16:12.190 --> 16:13.880
You're free to refuse.

16:13.880 --> 16:16.000
But I won't make this offer again.

16:17.500 --> 16:22.880
If you drop out due to dehydration now, 
you're guaranteed to lose to Horikita.

16:24.910 --> 16:27.370
Fine. I accept your trade.

16:27.370 --> 16:30.390
But how much food do you want?

16:30.390 --> 16:34.640
Half of the food you 
have left. It's a deal.

16:42.660 --> 16:44.650
You only have one left.

16:44.650 --> 16:47.160
This was "more water than you need"?

16:47.160 --> 16:50.160
Did you think I'd feel indebted 
to you if you saved me?

16:50.160 --> 16:52.160
If you hadn't looked into it,

16:52.160 --> 16:55.300
you wouldn't have felt 
indebted in the first place.

16:57.050 --> 17:00.040
Even if you were indebted, 
would you ever try to pay it back?

17:00.040 --> 17:01.360
Hell no.

17:02.170 --> 17:03.180
Okay.

17:18.600 --> 17:22.030
You arrived quite late, Ayanokoji.

17:23.670 --> 17:25.900
It does appear so.

17:25.900 --> 17:30.870
I was thinking I had a strong rival 
in my designated area arrivals.

17:30.870 --> 17:32.330
Would that have been you?

17:32.330 --> 17:34.320
I'm not really sure.

17:34.320 --> 17:38.040
Being in the same area doesn't 
mean we're on the same table.

17:38.390 --> 17:43.710
I thought you had no interest 
in being in the top ten,

17:43.990 --> 17:46.270
but this morning, 
you were suddenly in 9th.

17:51.560 --> 17:55.210
This deserted island test 
has just been so much fun.

17:55.590 --> 17:58.810
I've found myself as excited as a child.

17:59.140 --> 18:02.810
I intend to keep going at 
this pace a bit longer.

18:02.810 --> 18:04.810
You're not aiming for number one?

18:05.190 --> 18:08.660
The top three slots are already 
set up to be a bloodbath.

18:08.980 --> 18:15.320
Though I might reconsider if Nagumo 
or Koenji starts to collapse.

18:15.320 --> 18:17.860
Collapse?

18:17.860 --> 18:21.200
That seems very unlikely at the moment.

18:21.520 --> 18:24.970
You think Nagumo will just allow 
Koenji's dominance to stand?

18:25.470 --> 18:26.750
They could even end up

18:26.750 --> 18:30.820
in a situation where they both 
struggle to acquire more game points.

18:30.820 --> 18:34.720
Taking down rivals is also an 
important part of the battle.

18:34.960 --> 18:37.350
You're not aiming for the top spots?

18:37.350 --> 18:41.600
Unfortunately, it seems unlikely 
that I'll even crack the top ten.

18:41.600 --> 18:43.290
Really?

18:43.290 --> 18:47.860
It seems to me you've been racking 
up points at the same rate I have.

18:48.310 --> 18:51.550
A lot of groups will be losing 
efficiency by this point.

18:51.550 --> 18:53.920
You just have to keep at it.

18:53.920 --> 18:56.780
The bottom ten groups would 
love that, wouldn't they?

18:56.780 --> 19:00.370
They'd want to see any 
other group drop out.

19:00.620 --> 19:05.460
When a person gets desperate, 
they become capable of anything.

19:05.460 --> 19:07.130
Don't let your guard down.

19:07.470 --> 19:11.880
As a girl, I think you're the one 
who should be worried about that.

19:14.190 --> 19:18.910
I suppose a beautiful maiden 
such as myself should be more wary.

19:19.390 --> 19:24.640
<i>I meant it as a joke, but she seems 
to be seriously considering it.</i>

19:24.640 --> 19:27.150
If it comes up, yes...

19:27.370 --> 19:30.400
I suppose I'll force my way through.

19:30.400 --> 19:33.900
<i>That answer isn't maidenly at all.</i>

19:34.270 --> 19:36.780
Sorry to take up your time.

19:36.780 --> 19:38.840
You're not going to the challenge?

19:38.840 --> 19:41.990
You could probably still 
register if you hurry.

19:41.990 --> 19:43.980
I don't think so.

19:43.980 --> 19:47.120
I doubt I could beat the upperclassmen.

20:00.140 --> 20:02.190
Yume-chan?

20:02.190 --> 20:05.140
T-Takemoto-kun?

20:05.560 --> 20:06.910
Where are you?

20:07.560 --> 20:08.900
Yume-chan?!

20:10.150 --> 20:12.900
No, I'm afraid I'm not Yume.

20:14.110 --> 20:16.900
Um, Ayanokoji-kun...

20:17.120 --> 20:18.420
Good evening.

20:18.420 --> 20:21.760
Shiranami? Where are Kobashi and Takemoto?

20:21.760 --> 20:23.390
Um, well...

20:23.800 --> 20:27.920
I was rushing to keep up when 
suddenly I didn't know where I was...

20:27.920 --> 20:32.720
Walking along aimlessly will 
just get you more lost.

20:32.720 --> 20:34.420
R-Right.

20:34.730 --> 20:36.490
Do you have stamina left?

20:36.980 --> 20:39.800
Let's try to meet up with them.

20:39.800 --> 20:43.810
I do, but... how?

20:43.810 --> 20:49.490
Use a GPS search and you can find 
their general direction and distance.

20:56.940 --> 20:59.670
Why are you helping me?

20:59.670 --> 21:04.410
One element of this test is that 
it's a battle between grade years.

21:04.410 --> 21:07.700
But you even used a GPS search...

21:07.700 --> 21:12.580
It's because you're in 
Ichinose's class, I suppose.

21:13.920 --> 21:17.590
Ayanokoji-kun, are you and Honami-chan...

21:18.910 --> 21:20.730
We're nothing.

21:20.730 --> 21:22.680
Chihiro-chan!

21:22.680 --> 21:24.280
Shiranami!

21:25.540 --> 21:27.720
Chihiro-chan!

21:28.420 --> 21:29.920
Where are you?

21:29.920 --> 21:32.840
Chihiro-chan! Where are you?!

21:32.840 --> 21:34.270
Yume-chan!

21:34.860 --> 21:37.400
Yume-chan!

21:39.470 --> 21:40.990
Chihiro-chan!

21:40.990 --> 21:42.110
Thank goodness!

21:42.430 --> 21:43.960
Are you all right?

21:42.430 --> 21:44.100
Thanks a lot, Ayanokoji.

21:44.100 --> 21:46.120
You really saved Shiranami back there.

21:46.350 --> 21:49.000
I do have a question for you.

21:50.250 --> 21:53.000
Do you happen to have a transceiver?

21:56.650 --> 21:57.750
First...

21:57.750 --> 22:00.760
Sakayanagi, I'd like to ask you a favor.

22:01.120 --> 22:03.930
<i>By all means, proceed.</i>

22:03.930 --> 22:08.280
<i>I'll gladly return the favor 
for the classmates you helped.</i>
